                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Second half of the seventeenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Fine, careful hand. The quality of the handwriting varies throughout the manuscript. On <locus from="72va" to="77vc"/> the
                           letters tend to be slenderer and taller. On <locus from="89ra" to="89vc"/> the letters are broadly spaced.</desc>
                        
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item><abbr>ምል፡</abbr> for <expan>ምልጣን፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ማኅ፡, ማኅሌ፡</abbr> for <expan>ማኅሌት፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>መዝሙ፡</abbr> for <expan>መዝሙር፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ቅንዋ፡</abbr> for <expan>ቅንዋት፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ቅኔ፡ ደብ፡</abbr> for <expan>ቅኔ፡ ደብተራ፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ይትባ፡, ዘይትባረ፡</abbr> for <expan>ይትባረክ፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ስብሐ፡</abbr> for <expan>ስብሐተ፡ ነግህ፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>እስመ፡ ለዓ፡</abbr> for <expan>እስመ፡ ለዓለም፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ቃለ፡ ዓ፡</abbr> for <expan>ቃለ፡ ዓዋዲ፡</expan></item>
                           <item><abbr>ሃ፡</abbr> for <expan>ሃሌሉያ፡</expan></item>
                        </list>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; name of the king; a few groups of lines (alternating with black lines) in the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>
